    <merge>
      <title>Modifying Kernel Boot Parameters</title>
      <!--subtitle>Subtitle if necessary</subtitle-->
      <!-- Create changelog to enable versioning; add most recent entries at the top. -->
      <revhistory xml:id="rh-kernel-boot-parameters-modify">
        <revision><date>2026-08-26</date>
          <revdescription>
            <itemizedlist>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  &sle; 16 has no &yast;. Permanent kernel boot parameter changes are made with the
                  <command>update-bootloader</command> command instead of the &yastcc; Boot Loader
                  module.
                </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  &sle; 16 uses SELinux by default instead of AppArmor.
                </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  <literal>linuxrc</literal> no longer exists on &sle; 16. Early-boot parameters
                  formerly associated with it are ordinary kernel boot parameters handled by
                  dracut.
                </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  <keycap>F10</keycap> and <keycombo><keycap function="control"/><keycap>X</keycap></keycombo>
                  both boot the edited &grub; entry. Recovering from a boot failure means
                  selecting the <literal>(recovery mode)</literal> entry under
                  <guimenu>Advanced options for &productnameshort; &productnumber;</guimenu>,
                  not a separate recovery mode.
                </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  Temporarily modifying kernel boot parameters, and recovering from a boot
                  failure, both require physical or remote console access; neither works over
                  SSH.
                </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  On many systems the &grub; menu is hidden by default and the saved entry boots
                  automatically. Press <keycap function="escape"/> while the &sle; boot logo is
                  showing to reveal the menu.
                </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  Test a parameter temporarily before making it permanent, to confirm it has the
                  effect you expect.
                </para>
              </listitem>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  If no pre-modification backup exists, you can still recover from a boot failure
                  by removing the offending parameter directly from recovery mode.
                </para>
              </listitem>
            </itemizedlist>
          </revdescription>
        </revision>
        <revision><date>2025-11-04</date>
          <revdescription>
            <para>
              Initial version
            </para>
          </revdescription>
        </revision>
      </revhistory>
